<title>FRANCE: FIRS puts French 96/97 sugar output at 4.23 mln T.</title>
<headline>FIRS puts French 96/97 sugar output at 4.23 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>France produced 4.226 million tonnes of beet sugar in 1996/97, provisional statistics from French sugar intervention board FIRS showed.</p>
<p>That compared with 4.199 million tonnes of sugar produced in 1995/96.</p>
<p>In its February report FIRS said an increase in the crop's sugar content helped offset a drought-induced decline in beet weight per hectare.</p>
<p>The estimate assumed an area of 422,000 hectares and a sugar yield of 10.01 tonnes per hectare, compared with area of 430,000 ha and yield of 9.77 tonnes in 1995/96.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
